[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mulss  -12(%rbp), %xmm0     ; * prev
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m movss  -20(%rbp), %xmm1     ; sum
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m addss  %xmm1, %xmm0         ; destination is the PRODUCT, not sum
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m i.e. `product + sum`, not `sum + product`. The translation had
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `fadd(sum, product)`. Fixed in `src/perlin.rs` for all three of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stb_perlin_ridge_noise3`, `stb_perlin_fbm_noise3` and
