[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bytes, chosen below 192 so that the derived `basis` index stays inside the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mapped pages — that is the majority outcome (a uniform byte is below 192 with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m probability 3/4). The bytes that *are* stable (the low byte of each pointer, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0x7f` / `0x00` in the top three) are reproduced exactly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    195[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    196[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/differential.rs` deliberately contains no input that reads these 18
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    197[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bytes, and the fuzzing scripts treat a C program that disagrees with itself
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    198[0m:[38;5;10m[49m across repeated runs as "not a mismatch".
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    199[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
